  "steps": [
    "Shred the jackfruit with two forks, discarding any tough core, until it looks like pulled meat.",
    "Soften the onion in oil for 8 minutes, then add garlic and smoked paprika and cook for one minute.",
    "Add the jackfruit and fry for 5 minutes to catch some colour, then stir in the passata, maple, soy and vinegar.",
    "Simmer for 15 minutes, adding splashes of water, until sticky and deeply flavoured. Shred any larger pieces further.",
    "Pile into toasted buns with quick slaw and pickles. Napkins mandatory."
  ],
  "notes": "Make sure to buy jackfruit in brine or water, never syrup. The filling reheats perfectly, so it's a great one to make a day ahead."
}
